  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Located in the heart of the Netherlands, Wittenborg University of Applied Sciences is a vocational university recognised by the Dutch government. It was founded in 1987 and provides higher-level bachelor's and master's degrees in vocational education.</p><ul><li>With its main office located in Apeldoorn, Wittenborg University of Applied Sciences is a vibrant business school that holds dual accreditation</li><li>It has more than 1500 students and staff representing over 100 nationalities</li><li>It is one of the few higher education institutions in the Netherlands that speaks only English</li><li>The University also maintains a bustling study centre in Amsterdam where you can concentrate on technology and entrepreneurship</li></ul>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<ul><li>The typical monthly room rent in the Netherlands is between €300 and €600, but this might vary based on the location, size, and amenities provided.</li><li>The University helps its students locate appropriate, nearby housing. In addition to the housing options provided by Wittenborg, students can also find affordable accommodations through the University's partners.</li></ul><p><strong>Accommodations for students in Apeldoorn:</strong></p><ul><li>There are plenty of rooms available in the central Netherlands city of Apeldoorn, which is home to Wittenborg's main campus and is also clean and safe. For all new students, Wittenborg provides accommodations on campus in the form of either independent studios for single occupancy or communal student housing.</li><li>Wittenborg inaugurated its new student living facilities on De Ruyterstraat 5, in January 2023. It has evolved into a cosy, safe haven for students coping with the housing crisis in the Netherlands.</li><li>De Ruyterstraat 5, which has 75 comfortable units with separate kitchens, bathrooms, showers, and toilets, is more than just a place to stay.</li><li>Additionally, the school has 70 rooms spread around Apeldoorn, accommodating 145 students’ apartments.</li></ul>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sports",
      "value": "<p>Wittenborg students participate actively in their own sports groups, which plan outdoor games like basketball and soccer in the local parks. During your orientation day at Wittenborg, you will gain access to a private Facebook page where staff and students will help you with your preparations.</p><p>There are numerous resources available in the city of Apeldoorn for you to engage in sports like:</p><ul><li>Hockey</li><li>Soccer</li><li>Tennis, Rugby, Golf, and Squash</li><li>Volleyball</li><li>Fitness and Gyms</li><li>Boxing, Karate, Tai Chi and other Martial Arts</li><li>Archery</li><li>Horse Riding</li><li>Swimming, Diving, Outdoor Rowing</li><li>Athletics and Running</li></ul>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
